Z||000005||Cheever3000||10-09-2001||09:47 AM||||My wife will probably try hard to talk me out of it, but for now I plan to go.  I figure why should I expect anybody to come visit me some day if I don't make the effort to visit them.<P>Fiero owners here in my town don't get together much.  It's really sad.  So I'm desperate for some human interaction with others who like these cars.  It was good to meet Socha, but knowing there are so many others out there makes me crazy.  <P>Now I'm going to stare at Grinthock's pics some more.  ~sigh~<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000006||JohnF||10-09-2001||10:01 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever3000:<BR><B><BR>Now I'm going to stare at Grinthock's pics some more.  ~sigh~</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Heh, Heh, Heh!  Make sure your wife isn't around&gt;<P>Looking forward to seeing you there.  When I was in Conroe this past weekend, I simply forgot to bring your ph. number (and we had guests everyday but Fri.)<P>My wife says we'll try to have some kind of free snacks along for the attendees, if we have an idea how many is coming.  <P>All must remember , though, no VISIBLE, open alcholic containers.  Of, course, drivers wouldn't have that as a problem, anyway! <P>||||reg||12
Z||000007||Cheever3000||10-09-2001||10:35 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>When I was in Conroe this past weekend, I simply forgot to bring your ph. number<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>By saying 'expecting people to visit me', I didn't mean when you were down here on other business.  No problem.  I was thinking of New Years maybe.  There won't be any event to speak of, just a get-together like you're having, but I hear the local Impala club has a good fireworks show then.  Apparently one of their members is rich and even has the required license to put on a bigtime show.  I'm trying to get us invited.<BR>||||reg||1
